<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hamad ibn Isa Al Khalifa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1872">1872</a>–<a href="/years/1942">1942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hamad ibn Isa Al <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalifa">Khalifa</a> was ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain</a> from 1932 to 1942, after acting as ruler from 1923 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> forced his father, Isa ibn Ali, to step aside. With the adviser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-belgrave">Charles Belgrave</a> he introduced administrative reforms, courts and schools. Oil was discovered in Bahrain in 1932, the first find on the Arab side of the Gulf.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hamad-ibn-isa-al-khalifa.jpg" alt="Hamad ibn Isa Al Khalifa" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DHSgov · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bilateral_Meeting_with_King_Hamad_bin_Isa_Al_Khalifa_-_54551307222_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
